From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0945 redfin: touch statistics; sectouchx (IRQ timestamps, READ_ALL, probe, priority)

Always on, nothing sent changes: sweet_sects.c prints every 5 s while
touching `SWEET SECTS: 5s: events N (moves M, batched B) rate R/s | dt
p50/p95/max ms | gaps>20ms G | irq->dispatch p50/p95 us | wake p50/p95 us |
per drain avg A max B (C us max) | x X` (sample time = the attention
interrupt), and SweetHID.cpp prints `SWEET HID: real|swipe: moves N dt
p5/p50/p95/max ms | gaps>20ms G | dispatch avg/max us` from the HID
timestamps iOS gets (5 s, or at lift after >= 10 moves).

sectouchx= (default 0 = as before):
 0x1 HID timestamp = the attention interrupt (sec_ts_isr), a finger's
     moves in one drain sent once at the newest position
 0x2 READ_ALL_EVENT for >= 3 queued events (left_event), 500 us wait
 0x4 read-only probe of SET_TOUCHFUNCTION (0x30) and SET_REPORT_RATE (0x34)
 0x8 touch thread at priority 92 (kernel default 81)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
